      "id": "far-jl-ledger-c3",
      "heading": "Example 4: posting to the ledger (Cash, Bank, Capital)",
      "explanation_md": "After the journal, each entry is posted to the two accounts it touches. The handwritten solution balances each account at the end (March 31, marked c/d for carried down).\n\n**Cash A/c.** Debit side: June 5 capital 2,00,000 and June 22 sales 15,000, total 2,15,000. Credit side: June 8 Bank 80,000, June 25 Gulmohar 30,000, June 30 Salary 6,000, total 1,16,000. **Balance c/d: 99,000** on the credit side, which brings the two sides level at 2,15,000.\n\n**Bank A/c.** Debit: June 8 cash 80,000 and June 28 Mohit Bros 10,000, total 90,000. Credit: June 12 machines 20,000 and June 18 rent 5,000, total 25,000. **Balance c/d: 65,000.**\n\n**Capital A/c.** Credit: June 5 cash 2,00,000. Balance c/d 2,00,000 on the debit side.",
